        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev, Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, Hamlet, King Claudius, Grigori Kozintsev\n- Roles: film actor, theater actor, aristocratic characters\n- Works: Hamlet\n- Topics: Shakespeare characters\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev was a Russian film and theater actor who lived from May 29, 1927, to January 26, 2008.\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions.\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev played Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet.\"\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are childhood friends of Hamlet.\n- King Claudius summoned Rosencrantz and Guildenstern to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and, if possible, discover its cause.",
